<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Eletropaulo started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Eletropaulo started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel said it had started coverage of Brazilian power distributor Eletropaulo SA with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Eletropaulo became an attractive investment opportunity after the new management took control,&quot; analyst Luciana Portolano wrote in a Monday report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Significant expense cutting and an austere program of restructuring have turned losses into profits, transforming the ugly duckling of the distribution sector into a swan.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company is likely to privatized in the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- The company's shares rose 3.50 to 135 reais in Sao Paulo on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street Desk (212) 859-1730</p>
</text>
